! ADDRESS INVALID IS A NO-OP THAT FETCHES NOTHING -- prepareExec's AD
! clause, for all three classes it covers, and the VFL/connective AD
! that the model did not have until this deck found it missing.
!
! THE RULE.  Reference Manual printed p.21 (PDF 24), read at the ink:
!   "When an effective word address is obtained which does not
!   correspond to a core storage location that is physically available
!   in a particular installation, indicator AD, address invalid, is
!   turned on.  An instruction with an invalid data address is executed
!   as a NO OPERATION instruction."
! printed p.45 item 16 (PDF 48) repeats it for "the location specified by
! the effective operand address of the instruction just attempted".
! The installation here is StretchMemory's InstalledWords, 98,304 words;
! (8)400000.0 is word 131,072.
!
! THE CLAUSE.  StretchIBox.prepareExec calls such an instruction
! "completes without fetch": its look-ahead level gets no operand
! address.  The machine's own mechanism is the level's NOOP tag (Perf.
! Char. Vol. 1 printed A-8, PDF 67, "NOOP no-op bit"), which the TBC
! tests to suppress the operation (docs/spec_lookahead.md section 2.7).
!
! >>> MODEL BUG FOUND AND FIXED, 2026-11-18. <<<  Only the Fp arm of
! execute() asked installed().  A VFL L or a connective C at (8)400000.0
! did NOT set AD (this deck hung at its first BZB, $AD) -- prepareExec
! promised a completion execute() never performed.  vflIntOp and
! connectiveOp now set AD and skip the whole operation, the same
! "nothing at all" their DF guard does (immediate and CV excluded).
!
! WHERE THE FETCH WOULD COST.  Each refused instruction follows six
! I-box-only LVIs, so the E-box is idle and a level waiting for an
! operand word shows in the total.  AD is set-only in the model (bits
! 0-19 cannot be cleared), so only the FIRST case checks AD; every case
! checks a value witness: the accumulator still holds PAT, and a
! PROGRESSIVE store or connect-to-memory leaves its index register
! unadvanced (a no-op does no indexing).  The stored word itself cannot
! witness anything: StretchMemory drops a write past installed core and
! returns zero for a read.
!
! CYCLES 562 IS MODEL BEHAVIOUR, not a documented time: the manual says
! only "executed as a NO OPERATION", and Perf. Char. prints no time for a
! no-op'd level.  (The fetch is cheap here because StretchMemory answers
! a read past installed core at once, with zero.)
!
! INJECTIONS, each made alone in StretchIBox.bsv (or StretchExecute.bsv)
! from a saved copy, run across all three cwf_ decks, restored and
! compared with cmp -- OBSERVED on this final deck:
!   VflInt !installed clause dropped     -> CYCLES 563, nothing else
!   Connective !installed clause dropped -> CYCLES 565, nothing else
!   Fp !installed clause dropped         -> CYCLES 563, nothing else
!   vflIntOp's new AD guard removed      -> PC 396 (the first BZB, $AD
!                                           hang), CYCLES 136
!   connectiveOp's new AD guard removed  -> PC 412 (the BZB, $AE after
!                                           C0011: it loaded zero), 262
! (the five X0 and DF clause injections leave this deck at 562.)
        SLC, (8)300.0
START   BB, $AD, $                   ! hang if AD is on before anything
        L(BU,64,8), PAT              ! the accumulator PRELOAD
        LVI, $X2, 1                  ! I-box only: the E-box drains
        LVI, $X2, 2
        LVI, $X2, 3
        LVI, $X2, 4
        LVI, $X2, 5
        LVI, $X2, 6
        L(BU,64,8), (8)400000.0      ! VFL L, word 131072: AD, no-op
        BZB, $AD, $                  ! hang if AD did not come on
        K(BU,64,8), PAT
        BZB, $AE, $                  ! hang if the load landed
        LVI, $X2, 1
        LVI, $X2, 2
        LVI, $X2, 3
        LVI, $X2, 4
        LVI, $X2, 5
        LVI, $X2, 6
        C0011(BU,64), (8)400000.0    ! connective C: no-op
        K(BU,64,8), PAT
        BZB, $AE, $                  ! hang if the connect landed
        LVI, $X2, 1
        LVI, $X2, 2
        LVI, $X2, 3
        LVI, $X2, 4
        LVI, $X2, 5
        LVI, $X2, 6
        LV, $X3, BAD                 ! X3's value field := (8)400000.0
        ST(V+I)(BU,6,6), .1($X3)     ! progressive VFL store: no-op, so
        KV, $X3, BAD                 !   X3 must NOT advance
        BZXE, $
        CM0011(V+I)(BU,6), .1($X3)   ! progressive connect to memory: same
        KV, $X3, BAD
        BZXE, $
        LVI, $X2, 1
        LVI, $X2, 2
        LVI, $X2, 3
        LVI, $X2, 4
        LVI, $X2, 5
        LVI, $X2, 6
        L(U), (8)400000.0            ! floating point L: no-op
        LVI, $X2, 1
        LVI, $X2, 2
        K(BU,64,8), PAT
        BZB, $AE, $
        B, PASS
PASS    BEW, $
        CNOP
        SLC, (8)400.0
PAT     DD(BU,64,8), (8)0000125252525212525240
BAD     VF, (8)400000.0
        END, START
